Extended `enable_plan` and `enable_deploy` gating to config plan generation and deployment. Devices whose winning Setting has the feature disabled are skipped with an `E3038` warning naming the Setting and weight; jobs with no eligible devices log a single `E3039` warning. Both the `Deploy Config Plans` job and the `Deploy Config Plan` Job Button Receiver apply the same gate.
Moved the `enable_sotagg` and `enable_postprocessing` toggles to the per-`GoldenConfigSetting` flags so they are resolved from each device's winning Setting. Intended configuration postprocessing (in both the UI/API render action and config deployment) is now gated by the winning Setting's `enable_postprocessing` flag, and the SoT Aggregation UI action and API endpoint are gated by the winning Setting's `enable_sotagg` flag, instead of the global plugin settings.
